.TH HTTPSTEST 1
.SH NAME
httpstest \- live test of the HTTPS client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B httpstest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Httpstest
exercises
.IR https (2)
against the real network:
.IP 1.
a GET of a public Bluesky API endpoint,
.B by hostname
\(em exercising the
.B $Srv
resolver fallback (no
.I /net/cs
runs in this emu instance, the gap
.IR dialtest (1)
recorded) and a
.B Content-Length
response;
.IP 2.
a GET of
.BR mastodon.social 's
instance endpoint \(em a larger response, whichever framing the
server picks (the framing actually seen is printed, so a PASS says
which code paths really ran);
.IP 3.
a request for a nonexistent endpoint, which must come back as an HTTP
error
.I status
with a body and a nil error \(em APIs put their diagnostics in
error-status bodies, so treating 4xx as failure would break every
caller;
.IP 4.
a nonexistent hostname, which must fail with a resolution error;
.IP 5.
offline, via the module's own test seam: the chunked transfer-coding
decoder must decode a multi-chunk body exactly (with a chunk
extension and a trailer, and with multi-digit sizes \(em an early
negative control corrupted the size arithmetic and all-single-digit
chunks sailed through, so both a two-decimal-digit and a hex-letter
size are pinned), must reject a truncated body, and must reject a
garbage size line. The live hosts all answer with
.B Content-Length
today, so this path is unreachable over the network;
.IP 6.
a literal-IP
.B https
URL, which must fail
.I "certificate verification"
end to end \(em the URL's host is the verification hostname and no
public certificate names a bare IP address. This drives the full
wrong-certificate path through
.IR https (2)
itself, not just through
.IR x509 (2)
the way
.IR tls12test (1)'s
controls do.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/httpstest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR https (2),
.IR tls12test (1),
.IR bskytest (1),
.IR mastotest (1)
.SH BUGS
Needs the real network and real third-party servers; a failure can
mean the world changed rather than the code. The read-to-close
framing path has no live leg (every host tested sends
.BR Content-Length ).
